 <objectgroup id="3" name="areas_dialog">
  <object id="16" name="dialog_1" x="159.39" y="199.898" width="65.9782" height="90.1016">
   <properties>
    <property name="active_status" type="bool" value="true"/>
    <property name="dialogo" value="Arquimedes: Nesta etapa você vai dominar os teoremas de Thévenin e Norton.;Arquimedes: Thévenin substitui a rede por uma fonte de tensão Vth em série com Rth.;Arquimedes: Norton substitui a rede por uma fonte de corrente In em paralelo com Rn.;Arquimedes: As relações são Rth igual a Rn, Vth igual a In vezes Rth e In igual a Vth dividido por Rth.;Arquimedes: Para achar Vth, retire a carga e calcule a tensão de circuito aberto.;Arquimedes: Para achar Rth, desligue as fontes independentes e veja a resistência vista dos terminais.;Arquimedes: Para Norton, use a corrente de curto-circuito nos terminais para obter In.;Arquimedes: Sempre use GND Ground como referência de zero volt para as medições.;Arquimedes: Sem GND, os resultados podem ficar indefinidos ou incorretos.;Arquimedes: Nos painéis, identifique os terminais, calcule o equivalente e valide com cuidado."/>
    <property name="dialogo_en" value="Archimedes: In this stage you are going to master Thévenin's and Norton's theorems.;Archimedes: Thévenin replaces the network with a voltage source Vth in series with Rth.;Archimedes: Norton replaces the network with a current source In in parallel with Rn.;Archimedes: The relations are Rth equals Rn, Vth equals In times Rth, and In equals Vth divided by Rth.;Archimedes: To find Vth, remove the load and calculate the open-circuit voltage.;Archimedes: To find Rth, turn off the independent sources and look at the resistance seen from the terminals.;Archimedes: For Norton, use the short-circuit current at the terminals to obtain In.;Archimedes: Always use GND, Ground, as the zero-volt reference for measurements.;Archimedes: Without GND, the results may become undefined or incorrect.;Archimedes: On the panels, identify the terminals, calculate the equivalent, and validate carefully."/>
   </properties>
  </object>
 </objectgroup>
